invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: aes_runtime_test
reason: aes_traffic_key_load keeps the round count the stored schedule
  holds, so zero bytes, a wiped schedule's, would run the AES
  instructions at round count 0, and gcm_hw.c would read round key
  rounds - 1, far past the schedule. bin/aes_runtime_test loads zero
  bytes and reads the round count back.

--- old
    k->key.rounds = key_len == AES_256_KEY ? AES_256_ROUNDS : AES_128_ROUNDS;
--- new
    (void)key_len;
